Author: Muath Zahir <muathzaher2004@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Jul 28 04:43:26 2026 +0000

    ticket(4): waypoint cards that show the question, with an inline end-and-work confirm

    A waypoint row is now a card. Its first line is the type badge + title, its
    second the Work control, and expanding it reveals `question` — NOT NULL on the
    waypoints table, the single thing that session exists to answer, and rendered
    nowhere in the product until now — through <Markdown>, since it is agent-authored
    prose. Expanded cards also carry the resolved `summary` (also <Markdown>), the
    still-standing blocker titles, and the "surfaced by" lineage, all read off the
    `waypointGroups` derivation rather than recomputed here. Frontier cards start
    expanded (`item.expanded`); every other group starts collapsed.

    Work stops being refused in advance. The button is no longer disabled while a
    session is live, because after ticket 2 the server ends any session it can prove
    is finished and spawns anyway — so the ordinary handoff, including the initial
    grill that charted the map, is one click with no toast. Only a session genuinely
    mid-work still throws, and that refusal (GateError → PRECONDITION_FAILED) now
    renders as a confirm on the clicked card naming what would be ended, whose "End &
    work this" re-issues the same mutation with `endLive: true`. Research is excluded
    from the confirm entirely — it is a run, never refused for a live session — and
    any other error still toasts.

    Naming the blocker needs one new pure derivation, `liveSessionBlocker` in
    feature-ui.ts (tested there, no DOM): the live/launching session plus the title of
    the waypoint it still holds by claim. A resolved waypoint that merely remembers
    the session, and a waypoint claimed by a parallel research run, are both correctly
    not it. The mutation moved into the card (the `Lane` per-row pattern) so the
    confirm and the pending state belong to the card that was clicked.

    Two judgement calls: clicks inside `.wp-detail` stop propagating, so selecting the
    question's prose doesn't fold the card away — the first line and its caret stay
    the way to collapse; and Enter/Space only toggles when the card itself has focus,
    never when it bubbles up from the Work button.

    Verified: apps/web `tsc --noEmit` (the same 3 pre-existing errors in
    EnableAfkCard/SettingsOverlay, none new), `vite build`, root `bun run typecheck`,
    and `bun run test` — 750 pass, the one failure being dev-pane's process-tree kill,
    which fails identically on a clean tree in this container. The card's pixels are
    still unverified against prototype.html: no browser runs in this container.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

